,"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1023016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a05c239b1788d255988dd06437869b89fd82ab7f602b0068450df3f4dba00595","compact":"3ea90e6d8f2a2e206fa58d2edf0d346744d1547a909fce71a458ae268083f0e7","nasal":"3ea90e6d8f2a2e206fa58d2edf0d346744d1547a909fce71a458ae268083f0e7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-23-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":23,"verse":17,"english":"In days of yore, O Räma, on the occasion of the destruction of Vſtra, the thousand-eyed one came to have hunger, to be besmeared with excreta, and to slay a Brahmana.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-24-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1023017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3565b5728d29d8f2e99776160810feba2fa8d77596d3b4c0397f092235344955","compact":"8f429f30695e44aa41f67ade82bdcf04a666c91f16b3cfaec160284fc8268013","nasal":"8f429f30695e44aa41f67ade82bdcf04a666c91f16b3cfaec160284fc8268013"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-23-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":23,"verse":18,"english":"When Indra had been thus besmeared, the deities, and the saints having asceticism for wealth, washed him here, and cleansed his person from the dirt.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-24-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1023018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"52b37b0ebe53245b906fabb324678870edf56208ab8fee8479ef2b513521349b","compact":"dccb77db48779f711669b8f2e6b923be553158adf08a70e59e96e541c1f22ef0","nasal":"bf72de533c2cb9ebafcaddea14de833acb86c873c7eafdc40f17ad22bab438c2"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-23-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":23,"verse":19,"english":"And the deities, having renounced here the filth that had clung to the person of the mighty Indra, as well as his hunger, attained exceeding delight.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-24-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1023019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"53f084e34be471fb8c0775a1453c87ff218e23015ffb9aa2533e2588c556241e","compact":"39092431da1c80411ca52a58aa6e122dfb6e80d76e8c0cad1a440e0d509ef262","nasal":"f0b345333e075881e1be1ba60c14e3f254ba5763bf673fef94325c1eb9b01d9d"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-23-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":23,"verse":20,"english":"And thereat Indra becoming purified, attained his former brightness, and looked like to gold. And mightily pleased with this region, he conferred on it an excellent boon, saying, Since these two places have held excreta from my body, the going by the names of Maladā and Kārūsa, shall attain exceeding prosperity and fame among men.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.422,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-24-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1023020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"508602d02b0cf2cfa8a7f2e83c17d65cbe45eb8340e80e4aec774f583c86a93d","compact":"b203f45ecf283946a65863bfdd2dd7912813c52000e16fe40fdeb91b4a718acf","nasal":"bc2ba2b491e19637a47144d4457a1314aa8dae97d50106759b2329be4ac1efc4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-23-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":23,"verse":21,"english":"And thereat Indra becoming purified, attained his former brightness, and looked like to gold. And mightily pleased with this region, he conferred on it an excellent boon, saying, Since these two places have held excreta from my body, the going by the names of Maladā and Kārūsa, shall attain exceeding prosperity and fame among men.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.709,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-24-19"],"status":"unr